---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import HeroSection from '../../components/HeroSection.astro';
import StatCard from '../../components/StatCard.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="Why Iran?" lang="en">

  <HeroSection
    headline="Why Iran?"
    subtitle="The single most consequential act of American self-interest since the Louisiana Purchase"
  />

  <!-- Section 1: Energy Dominance -->
  <section class="py-20 md:py-28">
    <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-6">
      <p class="text-sm uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-gold font-bold text-center mb-3">Energy</p>
      <h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-black text-navy mb-12 text-center">Energy Dominance</h2>
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-6 mb-10">
        <StatCard
          number="208.6B"
          unit="Barrels of Proven Oil"
          description="3rd largest reserves in the world — 4.6x more than all 50 states combined"
          variant="navy"
        />
        <StatCard
          number="1,201 TCF"
          unit="Natural Gas"
          description="2nd largest reserves on Earth. Combined with US reserves, surpasses Russia."
          variant="white"
        />
      </div>
      <div class="prose prose-lg max-w-none text-gray-700">
        <p>
          Iran sits on the Strait of Hormuz, through which 27% of all seaborne oil passes every day. Under US sovereignty, that chokepoint becomes an American asset rather than a geopolitical vulnerability. OPEC's leverage over global energy markets is eliminated overnight.
        </p>
        <blockquote class="not-italic border-l-4 border-gold pl-6 my-8 text-xl font-bold text-navy">
          Sub-$2.50 gasoline becomes not a campaign promise, but an economic inevitability.
        </blockquote>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Section 2: The Debt Solution -->
  <section class="bg-navy py-20 md:py-28">
    <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-6">
      <p class="text-sm uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-gold font-bold text-center mb-3">Economy</p>
      <h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-black text-white mb-12 text-center">The Debt Solution</h2>
      <div class="max-w-md mx-auto mb-10">
        <StatCard
          number="$27.3T"
          unit="Natural Resource Wealth"
          description="Oil, gas, and mineral reserves valued at $27.3 trillion — enough to reshape the national balance sheet"
          variant="white"
          featured={true}
        />
      </div>
      <div class="text-lg text-gray-300 leading-relaxed space-y-6">
        <p>
          The United States carries $38.5 trillion in national debt. Iran's natural resource wealth offers a path to structural relief. Consider the precedent: Alaska's Permanent Fund, built on oil revenue, has accumulated $87.6 billion — generated by a state of just 733,000 people. Iran has 125 times that population, sitting on far greater reserves.
        </p>
        <p>
          Conservative estimates project <span class="text-gold font-bold">$150-200 billion per year</span> in new federal revenue from Iran's energy and mineral production alone. This is not a bailout. It is an acquisition that pays for itself.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Section 3: China Independence -->
  <section class="py-20 md:py-28">
    <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-6">
      <p class="text-sm uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-gold font-bold text-center mb-3">Security</p>
      <h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-black text-navy mb-12 text-center">China Independence</h2>
      <div class="max-w-md mx-auto mb-10">
        <StatCard
          number="68"
          unit="Mineral Types"
          description="Including rare earths critical to semiconductors, defense systems, and the energy transition"
          variant="navy"
        />
      </div>
      <div class="prose prose-lg max-w-none text-gray-700">
        <p>
          China controls over 80% of global rare earth processing — the materials essential to every smartphone, electric vehicle, fighter jet, and missile guidance system the United States builds. This is not a trade imbalance. It is a national security chokehold.
        </p>
        <blockquote class="not-italic border-l-4 border-gold pl-6 my-8 text-xl font-bold text-navy">
          No trade deal, no tariff, no diplomatic agreement achieves what sovereignty does.
        </blockquote>
        <p>
          Iran contains a 7,000 km&sup2; rare earth anomaly zone, one of the largest untapped deposits on Earth. Bringing Iran into the Union breaks China's monopoly and re-shores the most critical supply chain in the modern economy.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Section 4: Military Savings -->
  <section class="bg-navy py-20 md:py-28">
    <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-6">
      <p class="text-sm uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-gold font-bold text-center mb-3">Defense</p>
      <h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-black text-white mb-12 text-center">Military Savings</h2>
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-6 mb-10">
        <StatCard
          number="$8T"
          unit="Spent on Middle East Wars"
          description="The total cost of US military operations in the Middle East since 2001"
          variant="white"
        />
        <StatCard
          number="$20-50B"
          unit="Saved Per Year"
          description="Annual savings from eliminating the need for Gulf containment operations"
          variant="white"
        />
      </div>
      <div class="text-lg text-gray-300 leading-relaxed space-y-6">
        <p>
          The United States currently maintains over 40,000 troops across the Persian Gulf region for one primary purpose: containing Iran. The entire force posture is becoming both more expensive and less effective.
        </p>
        <p>
          Statehood resolves this permanently. Iran's 17 air bases become US military installations. The Fifth Fleet gains permanent, sovereign basing rights. The entire containment architecture becomes unnecessary. The savings are not theoretical. They are immediate and structural.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Section 5: Talent Pipeline -->
  <section class="py-20 md:py-28">
    <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-6">
      <p class="text-sm uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-gold font-bold text-center mb-3">Talent</p>
      <h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-black text-navy mb-12 text-center">Talent Pipeline</h2>
      <div class="max-w-md mx-auto mb-10">
        <StatCard
          number="335K"
          unit="STEM Graduates Per Year"
          description="5th largest producer of STEM talent globally — a workforce America desperately needs"
          variant="navy"
          featured={true}
        />
      </div>
      <div class="prose prose-lg max-w-none text-gray-700">
        <p>
          The United States has over 2 million unfilled STEM jobs. Iran produces 335,000 STEM graduates every year — and <strong>70% of its engineering graduates are women</strong>. This is not an immigration pipeline that requires visa lotteries. This is a domestic talent pool, integrated by constitutional right.
        </p>
        <p>
          Iranian-Americans are already the most educated immigrant group in the United States. The talent is proven. The question is scale.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Section 6: The Nuclear Solution -->
  <section class="bg-navy py-20 md:py-28">
    <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-6">
      <p class="text-sm uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-gold font-bold text-center mb-3">Nonproliferation</p>
      <h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-black text-white mb-12 text-center">The Nuclear Solution</h2>
      <div class="text-lg text-gray-300 leading-relaxed space-y-6">
        <p>
          Statehood is the only permanent solution to Iran's nuclear program. There is no treaty to renegotiate. No inspections to evade. No sunset clauses to expire. A state of the United States cannot have an independent nuclear weapons program — full stop.
        </p>
        <blockquote class="border-l-4 border-gold pl-6 py-2 text-2xl font-black text-white leading-snug my-8">
          Every other approach is temporary by design. They delay. Statehood resolves.
        </blockquote>
        <p>
          This single outcome may justify the entire cost of integration.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Section 7: Religion — The Data -->
  <section class="py-20 md:py-28">
    <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-6">
      <p class="text-sm uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-gold font-bold text-center mb-3">Religion</p>
      <h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-black text-navy mb-6 text-center">Iran Is Not What You Think</h2>
      <p class="text-lg text-gray-text text-center mb-16 max-w-3xl mx-auto">
        The Iranian government claims 99.98% of Iranians are Muslim. Anonymous surveys tell a radically different story.
      </p>

      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-8 mb-12">
        <!-- Official vs Reality -->
        <div class="bg-gradient-to-br from-red-900 to-red-950 rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h3 class="text-lg font-black text-red-300 mb-1">Official Government Census</h3>
          <p class="text-6xl font-black text-white mt-4">99.98%</p>
          <p class="text-red-200 mt-2">Muslim (government claims)</p>
          <p class="text-sm text-red-300/70 mt-4">Apostasy is punishable by death. The census has no option for "none." Everyone born to a Muslim family is counted as Muslim.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-gradient-to-br from-green-800 to-green-900 rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h3 class="text-lg font-black text-gold-light mb-1">GAMAAN Anonymous Survey (2020)</h3>
          <p class="text-6xl font-black text-white mt-4">40%</p>
          <p class="text-green-200 mt-2">Muslim (when asked anonymously)</p>
          <p class="text-sm text-green-300/70 mt-4">50,000+ respondents. Peer-reviewed. Published in Journal for the Scientific Study of Religion. Affiliated with Tilburg University.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Breakdown -->
      <div class="bg-gradient-to-br from-navy to-navy-light rounded-2xl p-8 md:p-10 mb-12">
        <h3 class="text-xl font-black text-gold mb-6 text-center">What Iranians Actually Believe</h3>
        <div class="grid grid-cols-2 md:grid-cols-4 gap-4">
          <div class="text-center">
            <p class="text-3xl font-black text-white">32%</p>
            <p class="text-sm text-gray-400 mt-1">Shi'ite Muslim</p>
          </div>
          <div class="text-center">
            <p class="text-3xl font-black text-white">22%</p>
            <p class="text-sm text-gray-400 mt-1">No religion</p>
          </div>
          <div class="text-center">
            <p class="text-3xl font-black text-white">9%</p>
            <p class="text-sm text-gray-400 mt-1">Atheist</p>
          </div>
          <div class="text-center">
            <p class="text-3xl font-black text-white">8%</p>
            <p class="text-sm text-gray-400 mt-1">Zoroastrian</p>
          </div>
          <div class="text-center">
            <p class="text-3xl font-black text-white">7%</p>
            <p class="text-sm text-gray-400 mt-1">Spiritual</p>
          </div>
          <div class="text-center">
            <p class="text-3xl font-black text-white">6%</p>
            <p class="text-sm text-gray-400 mt-1">Agnostic</p>
          </div>
          <div class="text-center">
            <p class="text-3xl font-black text-white">5%</p>
            <p class="text-sm text-gray-400 mt-1">Sunni Muslim</p>
          </div>
          <div class="text-center">
            <p class="text-3xl font-black text-white">11%</p>
            <p class="text-sm text-gray-400 mt-1">Other (Christian, Baha'i, Sufi, Humanist)</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Corroborating evidence -->
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-6 mb-12">
        <div class="border-2 border-gray-200 rounded-2xl p-6">
          <p class="text-3xl font-black text-navy">60%</p>
          <p class="text-sm text-gray-text uppercase tracking-widest mt-1">Don't fast for Ramadan</p>
          <p class="text-gray-text mt-3 text-sm">From Iran's <em>own government polling</em> (2020).</p>
        </div>
        <div class="border-2 border-gray-200 rounded-2xl p-6">
          <p class="text-3xl font-black text-navy">50,000</p>
          <p class="text-sm text-gray-text uppercase tracking-widest mt-1">Mosques closed</p>
          <p class="text-gray-text mt-3 text-sm">Out of 75,000 total. Iran has the lowest mosque attendance of any Islamic country.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="border-2 border-gray-200 rounded-2xl p-6">
          <p class="text-3xl font-black text-navy">70%</p>
          <p class="text-sm text-gray-text uppercase tracking-widest mt-1">Want separation of religion & state</p>
          <p class="text-gray-text mt-3 text-sm">The theocracy paradoxically secularized its own population.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <blockquote class="not-italic border-l-4 border-gold pl-6 my-8 text-xl font-bold text-navy">
        Adding Iran as a state would not shift America's religious demographics. Iran's population is more secular than its government — and more secular than many Americans assume.
      </blockquote>

      <p class="text-sm text-gray-text italic">
        Source: GAMAAN (Group for Analyzing and Measuring Attitudes in Iran), 2020. 50,000+ respondents. Peer-reviewed, published in the Journal for the Scientific Study of Religion. Affiliated with Tilburg University, Netherlands.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- CTA -->
  <section class="bg-navy py-20 md:py-28">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-6 text-center">
      <p class="text-lg text-gray-300 mb-6">The proof is already here — living in all 50 states.</p>
      <a
        href="/en/iranian-americans/"
        class="inline-block bg-gold text-navy font-black text-lg px-10 py-5 rounded-xl hover:bg-gold-light transition-colors shadow-lg shadow-gold/20"
      >
        Meet the Iranian-Americans
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>

</BaseLayout>
